      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve: enrich exported OTEL logs with stable semantics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators can keep OTEL diagnostic log bodies private today, but redacted records still need stable structure to be useful in Splunk or any OTEL sink. This PR makes ordinary `log.record` diagnostics and trusted `security.event` records queryable by stable event identity plus safe structured attributes without enabling broad log-body capture.\n\nThe stricter requirement is enforced here: OpenClaw-owned calls that emit OTEL `log.record` need intentional semantic context, not just generic exporter fallback enrichment. The remaining non-semantic surfaces are explicit pinned exemptions for console/progress/operator-output callbacks and true plugin/free-text forwarding boundaries.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDiagnostic log export now reserves OpenClaw-owned semantic fields before generic attributes: `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type`, and `openclaw.log.*` event/category/outcome/reason/site attributes. Spoofed generic attributes cannot replace those reserved meanings, and attribute-count pressure cannot drop the semantic fields.\n\nOrdinary logs remain redacted by default. Explicit call-site semantics win when present, subsystem/module/plugin/category metadata fills safe diagnostic semantics, and trusted `security.event` records stay separate from message-body semantics while adding `openclaw.security.<action>` event identity to the existing `openclaw.security.*` schema.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can query exported OpenClaw OTEL logs without parsing message text or enabling content capture. Diagnostic records now carry stable fields such as `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=log.record`, `openclaw.log.event`, `openclaw.log.category`, `openclaw.log.outcome`, `openclaw.log.reason`, `openclaw.log.site_id`, `openclaw.log.level`, and category/source metadata when available.\n\nSecurity events now use the same top-level event identity shape with `openclaw.signal.type=security.event`, while preserving the trusted security schema. Plugin/free-text logs remain compatible and private: raw message content is not used to infer event names or reason codes, and redacted diagnostic bodies still export as `[message redacted]` unless content capture is intentionally enabled.\n\nAccepted exemption boundary:\n\n- `operator_output_callback: 121` pinned call sites. These are console/progress/operator-output callbacks and are not converted in this PR.\n- `compat_runtime_adapter: 4` pinned call sites for compatibility runtime adapter logging.\n- Extension plugin/free-text fallback remains pinned by exact counts and fingerprints: `knownCount=382 knownFingerprint=8ed0750b44745cd1`, `injectedCount=428 injectedFingerprint=695ee489eac02cbb`.\n- Plugin logger adapter is not exempt; plugin/runtime logger metadata is wired through the structured logger API and covered by tests.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Redacted `log.record` exports include `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=log.record`, `openclaw.log.event`, `openclaw.log.category`, `openclaw.log.outcome`, `openclaw.log.reason`, and `openclaw.log.site_id` while keeping the body redacted.\n- Capture-enabled `log.record` exports keep the same event identity and semantic attributes while replacing only the body with the log message. This mode is tested only to prove conditional body behavior; it is not required or recommended for normal operation.\n- Trusted `security.event` exports include `eventName=openclaw.security.<action>`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=security.event`, `body=openclaw.security.event`, and the existing `openclaw.security.*` fields.\n- Exporter tests prove generic attributes cannot spoof reserved semantic keys or the trusted `openclaw.security.*` event namespace.\n- `src/logging/diagnostic-log-site-inventory.test.ts` audits OpenClaw-owned log sites across `src`, `extensions`, `packages`, and `ui`, and fails if owned OTEL-emitting logs lose explicit semantics, hide helper-generated event ids, reintroduce state/outcome in event names, or if pinned exemptions drift.\n\nRepresentative exported shapes:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"INFO\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.diagnostic.export\",\n  \"body\": \"[message redacted]\",\n  \"signalType\": \"log.record\",\n  \"event\": \"diagnostic.export\",\n  \"category\": \"diagnostic\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\",\n  \"reason\": \"configured\",\n  \"siteId\": \"0123456789abcdef\",\n  \"bodyRedacted\": true\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"INFO\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.heartbeat.runner\",\n  \"body\": \"[message redacted]\",\n  \"signalType\": \"log.record\",\n  \"event\": \"heartbeat.runner\",\n  \"category\": \"gateway.heartbeat\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\",\n  \"reason\": \"configured\",\n  \"bodyRedacted\": true\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"WARN\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.security.gateway.auth.failed\",\n  \"body\": \"openclaw.security.event\",\n  \"signalType\": \"security.event\",\n  \"action\": \"gateway.auth.failed\",\n  \"category\": \"auth\",\n  \"outcome\": \"denied\",\n  \"severity\": \"medium\",\n  \"reason\": \"token_mismatch\",\n  \"actorKind\": \"operator\",\n  \"targetKind\": \"gateway\",\n  \"policyDecision\": \"deny\",\n  \"controlFamily\": \"auth\"\n}\n```\n\nAutomated checks:\n\n- Focused regression bundle passed locally: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/diagnostic-log-site-inventory.test.ts src/logging/diagnostic-log-events.test.ts src/logger.test.ts src/logging/subsystem.test.ts src/logging/level-filter.test.ts src/plugins/logger.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-logging.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-logging.integration.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-llm.runtime.test.ts src/agents/command/attempt-execution.test.ts src/agents/tools/music-generate-tool.test.ts src/agents/provider-local-service.test.ts src/talk/logging.test.ts src/talk/agent-consult-runtime.test.ts src/talk/agent-talkback-runtime.test.ts src/plugins/services.test.ts src/tasks/task-registry.test.ts src/gateway/server-restart-sentinel.test.ts src/gateway/server-close.test.ts src/infra/restart.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/mentions.test.ts src/llm/providers/stream-wrappers/openai.test.ts` passed 8 shards / 482 tests.\n- Diagnostics exporter naming checks passed locally: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service.test.ts -t \"registers and removes an OTLP exporter unhandled rejection handler|uses a preloaded OpenTelemetry SDK without dropping diagnostic listeners\"` passed 2 tests.\n- Touched-module checks passed locally: sentinel, gateway close, restart, mentions, and OpenAI stream-wrapper tests passed 4 shards / 180 tests.\n- `corepack pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` passed after regenerating the plugin SDK API baseline hash for the updated plugin logger semantics.\n- `git diff --check` and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Focused structured review on `HEAD` completed clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Broad changed gate passed on Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox: provider `blacksmith-testbox`, id `tbx_01kwvkbr7xvk86zmqn2bk907bf`, Actions run `https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28788587510`, command `check:changed`, exit `0`.\n\nNo screenshots: this is backend/exporter/logging behavior and docs; there is no human-visible UI state to capture.\n",
